-- "An employee leaves and another takes over their shop", as one request. The
-- rule points the shop at the successor and deletes the employee who leaves.
-- The `never` reads `Shop.manager`, which the rule assigns, so it is read when
-- the commit ends. The request goes through when nothing is left pointing at
-- the departing employee. It is refused when the caller names one employee as
-- both, and when a second shop still points at the departing one.

act Employee {
    name: text
}

act Shop {
    name: text
    manager: one Employee
}

transient act ReplaceManager {
    shop: one Shop
    departing: one Employee
    successor: one Employee
}

never (ReplaceManager where departing is held)

rule ApplyReplace when ReplaceManager {
    shop.manager = successor
    delete departing
}
